+# Implement the native LAF adaptation-prep phase (P0 skeleton → P4 root pointer)
+
+## Task Overview
+
+This task implements the native LAF adaptation-prep phase specified in the design pack at `docs/native-prep/design/` (DESIGN.md + prep-agent-schemas.md + prep-skill-specs.md + path-contract.md + package-schemas.md + boundary-verification.md). The design is complete, user-approved (command placement confirmed 2026-07-04), and cross-validated against live code with **zero CODE-CONTRADICTED claims** (research/05), so the design pack is a faithful build spec that can be followed verbatim — except the two documented staleness corrections below (Narnia→Tolkien; runtime-vs-build-time promotion).
+
+The work is structured as the **five DESIGN.md §7 phases (P0–P4)** plus a Phase 1 setup phase — **six `### Phase` sections total**. The five DESIGN.md §7 phases are: **P0 Skeleton** (create 9 new files + hand-add 3 VENDOR rows), **P1 Body edits** (additive diffs to `analyst.md` and `tier-coordinator.md`), **P2 Commands** (`/laf:prep` + `/laf:rewrite`), **P3 Prove** (run the Tolkien prep end-to-end through greenlight + handoff — the HARD GATE), and **P4 Root pointer** (the ADDING_NEW_WORKS.md pointer paragraph). Every build/edit phase ends with a lens-based QA gate (M3), and P3 additionally runs a source-document fidelity gate (M4, I21) because the phase transforms a novel into a package that must faithfully realize the path-contract + package-schemas contract.
+
+The primary validation throughout is the boundary check: `uv run python laf-adaptation/scripts/check_boundary.py` (Mode V, no `--upstream`) must end with the line `BOUNDARY CONTRACT: PASS`. This project is a prompt + YAML-config framework, NOT software (ADR-006) — there are no unit tests; verification is the boundary check plus the P3 end-to-end prove.
+
+**Two documentation-staleness corrections are baked into this task and MUST be honored:** (1) DESIGN.md §7 P3 names Narnia (`--work narnia`), but the repo ships NO Narnia source/mapping — the P3 prove MUST use the committed Tolkien fixture strings instead. (2) The dual-form mapping promotion (`<slug>_mapping.yaml` root 5-key meaning-stripped + `<slug>-mapping.yaml` kb 6-key meaning-kept) is RUNTIME behavior of the prep-cordinator on greenlight via `/kb-management` — it is NOT a build-time file this task hand-creates; those files first appear when `/laf:prep` runs in P3.
+
+## Key Objectives
+
+The following objectives MUST be achieved by this task:
+
+1. **P0 — Native skeleton lands and the boundary stays green:** Create the 9 new native files (1 agent, 2 SKILL.md, 1 path-contract resource, 3 exemplars, 2 commands), hand-add the 3 NATIVE VENDOR rows, and prove `check_boundary.py` (Mode V) returns `BOUNDARY CONTRACT: PASS` with `--report` NATIVE count = 8 (baseline 5 + 3).
+2. **P1 — Additive body edits without adopted-body drift:** Apply the `analyst.md` (NATIVE) and `tier-coordinator.md` (BUILD-NEW) additive diffs, then prove the boundary is green AND `git diff --stat -- laf-adaptation/agents/writer.md laf-adaptation/agents/muse.md` is EMPTY (adopted bodies byte-unchanged).
+3. **P2 — The two /laf commands are well-formed:** Author `.claude/commands/laf/prep.md` + `rewrite.md` as thin delegators and prove each carries exactly one `description:` frontmatter line.
+4. **P3 — End-to-end prove on the Tolkien fixture (HARD GATE):** Run `/laf:prep "The Lord of the Rings" --source laf-adaptation/source/tolkien/ch-01.txt` through greenlight (slug `tolkien`) then `/laf:rewrite --work tolkien`, and prove the 8-file package, the meaning/compound_scene fields, the dual-form promotion (root 5-key meaning-absent / kb 6-key meaning-present), the hardcoded-path rewrite handoff, and a green boundary — passing the source-document fidelity gate (M4).
+5. **P4 — Root pointer + finalize:** Add the ADDING_NEW_WORKS.md pointer paragraph, run the final consolidated QA gate, run the POST reflect wrapper, and mark the task Done.
